## Install

```sh
php artisan module:add {{ Module }}
php artisan migrate
php artisan route:clear && composer typescript
```

## API

| Method | Path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/v1/{{ kebabPlural }}` | Paginated, `?search=` filters by name |
| POST | `/api/v1/{{ kebabPlural }}` | |
| GET | `/api/v1/{{ kebabPlural }}/{id}` | |
| PUT | `/api/v1/{{ kebabPlural }}/{id}` | Partial payloads accepted |
| DELETE | `/api/v1/{{ kebabPlural }}/{id}` | |

All routes are behind `auth:sanctum`. Add a `can:` gate in `Routes/api.php` if
this surface needs one, and define that gate in the PROJECT — who counts as an
administrator is a project decision, not a module's.

## Before you ship this

- [ ] Replace the placeholder `name` column with the real schema.
- [ ] Decide whether any of this needs a permission gate.
- [ ] If the module needs something a project must supply (an SMS channel, a
      tenant scope, an audience), declare a **contract** and ship a safe default
      rather than assuming another module is installed. See the `OtpChannel` /
      `SavedViewScope` / `CommentableRegistry` seams for the pattern.
- [ ] Fire **events** rather than calling another module directly.
- [ ] Run `bin/lint` from the modules repo before committing.

